From d6f4b17a74aaa7890e81aacfbfc08338f084f8e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Colliers <mail@thomascolliers.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 22:37:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] media: qcom: camss: add SM7635 resources and compatible

Add the resources for the SM7635 CAMSS complex, comprising four CSIPHY
v2.2.1, three CSID665 and three TFE665 instances, and expose it through
the qcom,milos-camss compatible.

The topology and per-instance clock assignments are derived from the
published downstream platform/vendor/qcom/proprietary/camera-devicetree
sources for SM7635 and cross-checked against camcc-milos. The downstream
camera-kernel cam_tfe665.h and cam_tfe_csid665.h register descriptions
identify the hardware revisions and layouts.

CSID665's RDI layout matches the existing csid_ops_340 implementation,
and CSIPHY v2.2.1 uses csiphy_ops_3ph_1_0 with the SM7635 register table.
TFE665 uses the vfe_ops_665 implementation. Base the resource rate tables
and interconnect votes on QCM2290's TFE CAMSS resources, extending them
to match the SM7635 block count and clock tree.

The soc_ahb clock gates the register-access AHB bus and is required for
the ISP registers to be reachable.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Colliers <mail@thomascolliers.com>
